 "author": "Rally Raid samples",
 "description": "Patterned after the Dakar's classic \"road to the coast\" stages (and the Namibia rounds of past African rallies): a fast gravel run down the C39 from the park gate through the Koigab valley to the Atlantic, a camp-site speed zone at Torra Bay, then an off-piste navigation section north over gravel plains and the Uniab delta before rejoining the C34 to Terrace Bay. Realistic: navigation waypoints (WPN) where there is no track, a WPS at the soft river crossing, speed zone through the camp, masked waypoints on the fast road to stop corner-cutting.",
